    "id": "q08",
    "question": "Why could a movement start above the thermal block limit on SMC-3?",
    "answer": {
      "found": true,
      "answer": "The thermal model updated its estimate in a 100 ms task, but the block decision read the estimate at the start of a movement, before that task had run with the newest current samples. So one movement could start on a stale value, which in endurance testing was 3 °C above the block limit. The fix was to read the estimate after the thermal task has run in the same cycle.",
      "quotes": [
        {
          "document": "LL-2024-01-thermal-check.md",
          "text": "The thermal model updated its estimate in a 100 ms task. The block decision read the estimate at the start of a movement, before the task had run with the newest current samples. One movement could start on a stale value."
        },
        {
          "document": "LL-2024-01-thermal-check.md",
          "text": "The block decision reads the estimate after the thermal task has run in the same cycle."
        }
      ]
    },
