    "id": "q09",
    "question": "What caused lost status frames in WLC-100 diagnostic sessions?",
    "answer": {
      "found": true,
      "answer": "During a diagnostic session, long diagnostic responses filled the CAN transmit queue, so a status frame that was due at that moment was dropped instead of being delayed. This showed up as gaps of about 100 to 150 ms, seen only in the service workshop. The fix was a larger transmit queue and a separate transmit buffer for status frames.",
      "quotes": [
        {
          "document": "LL-2024-09-can-frame-loss.md",
          "text": "During a diagnostic session, long diagnostic responses filled the CAN transmit queue. A status frame due at that moment was dropped instead of being delayed."
        },
        {
          "document": "LL-2024-09-can-frame-loss.md",
          "text": "The transmit queue was enlarged, and status frames got their own transmit buffer."
        }
      ]
    },
